      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "2006 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Secondary prevention of plaque rupture following percutaneous coronary intervention in patients with acute coronary syndrome is not well studied. This case report describes a 53-year-old man who experienced plaque rupture between two previously successfully implanted stents in the right coronary artery, as documented during the 3rd intervention using intravascular ultrasound."
      },
